					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-06 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><div align="center"><strong>NO LABEL (ESMA REMIX) :: VIDEO<br />Gabriel Teodros<br /></strong></div><br />Whattup ya&#39;ll... the first video from the Lovework album is done! check it out...<br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/29Vi46H7M-c"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/29Vi46H7M-c"></param><br /><param name="wmode" value="transparent"></param><br /></object><br /><br />Thank you to <strong>Zia</strong>,<strong> Johnny</strong>,<strong> Jelani</strong>,<strong> Fusae</strong>,<strong> MassLine</strong>,<strong> Sabzi</strong> for the remix, <strong>Moka Only</strong> for the original song, my neighbors and family who helped out, my entire musical family that came through to support, all the youth from <strong>Mercer Middle School</strong>, <strong>WAPIFASA</strong>, <strong>FGCP</strong>, <strong>Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center</strong>, and the entire neighborhood of <strong>Beacon Hill</strong> for raising me and allowing this whole video to be shot between the Jose P. Rizal Bridge and South Dawson Street. 206up!<br /><br />-GTeezy<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-05 | Tuesday</font></strong><br><br>pictured: Evan Flory-Barns, Ahamefule Oluo, D&#39;Vonne Lewis, Josh Rawlings<br /><strong><br />DON&#39;T MISS THE NEW &quot;MASSLINE PRESENTS&quot; EVENT!!!</strong><br /><br />Beautiful things are happening in Seattle and it is time for a celebration of what our great city has to offer. For 2 nights at the Langston Hughes Center for Performing Arts we are pulling out all of the stops and presenting <strong>The New Seattle Orchestra</strong>, a 20+ piece orchestra consisting of some of the most innovative performers in Seattle including <strong>Paul Rucker, Izaak Mills, Owour Arunga, Dylan Rieck, D&#39;Vonne Lewis, Jacques Willis, Eric Peters, Beth Fleenor</strong> and many others performing the works of <strong>Evan Flory-Barnes</strong> and <strong>Ahamefule J. Oluo</strong> with special guests of <strong>RA Scion</strong> of Common Market and <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> who will actually be performing with the orchestra. Comedian <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong> and <strong>Sabzi</strong> (Blue Scholars, Common Market) will be hosting this event. This will be a night to remember! <br /><br /><br /><strong>The New Seattle Orchestra</strong><br />Featuring: The Modern Orchestral Works of <strong>Evan Flory-Barnes</strong> and <strong>Ahamefule J. Oluo</strong> w/special guests <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> and <strong>RA Scion</strong> of Common Market.<br /><br />Langston Hughes Performing Arts Center<br />104 17th Ave S. Seattle, WA 98144<br /><strong><br />FRIDAY / June 15th &amp; <br />SATURDAY /June 16th<br />8pm All Ages</strong>
<br /><strong>$15 presale / $18 door</strong><br /><br />BUY TICKETS <strong><u><a href="http://www.brownpapertickets.com/event/16664">HERE</a></u></strong><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-02 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Peace. It&#39;s June already? Daaamn. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">5300+ miles on the odometer. It&#39;s day 18 of the tour and we finally found an internet spot at the Bend, Oregon public library. Saba just hipped yall with the sessions we had with some dope bay area youth. Thanks for riding with us!</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">(Thanks to daps1 for the updates in our absence! LOST Flash Forwards - ahhh shit!)  </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">The first ever MASSLINE Tour is about to come to an end. So that means it&#39;s shoutout time. For the fam who we left to go and rep for, who broke bread with us on the last night before departure, who shouldered our tasks back home and kept us updated and connected - we couldn&#39;t do this without you. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Shoutout to all the NW-erners in each and every last city we hit - keep carrying the torch for the region wherever you&#39;re at! And all the folks who put us up in their cribs, cooked us meals, guided us through traffic, came out to the shows, gave us free coffee (peace to Alma in SD!), gave us free other unmentionable stuff, hit up the in-stores, venue staff, all the folks I&#39;ve reconnected with after a hot minute - THANK YOU. Maraming salamat sa inyong lahat with rev love and fire for the people. </p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; min-height: 14px; margin: 0px">&nbsp;</p><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Stay tuned for video and audio of the trip. Oh, and our new music video for &quot;Back Home&quot; filmed by Zia Mohajerjasbi!</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-02 | Saturday</font></strong><br><br>big up to all the SF heads from Concord to East Oakland that came thru and showed love the last couple days.<br /><br />extra shouts go to &quot;hozay,&quot; manuel (that kid can dance), chris for filiming, detective blacksmith joe, all the underagers that snuck into pier 23, all the SoMa United Playaz heads from Rudy to Juice (it takes the Hood to save the Hood), ya&#39;ll made our trip to the Yay moreso the truth than could have been expected.<br /><br />shouts to Kiwizzo, Jasen, Bambu and his Bay Area release party, Beatrock, and all our other Cali fammos that we got a chance to connect with as well.<br /><br />happy grad Ahmed.&nbsp; you&#39;re a good performer.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-06-01 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>big up to all the folks who came out to Pier 23 to check the show last night!<br /><br />for those who&#39;ve been asking, the answer is yes.<br /><br />there will be a spontaneous MassLine appearance at the SoMa Recreation Center in SF. 270-6th St @ Folsom St! 4:30pm!<br /><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> [32] <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=245">[50]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=250">[51]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?